<title>PERU: Peru's February wheat output jumps to 519 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Peru's February wheat output jumps to 519 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's February wheat production rose to 519 tonnes from 162 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Production for the first two months of the year, however, fell to 569 tonnes compared with 1,764 tonnes in the same period last year, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in February fell 28.6 percent to $11.73 million, while in the first two months imports fell 12.6 percent to $31.26 million, the report added.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
